@1629[end]. Their habitations will be changed into more pleasant ones.

@1759. The fluidity and pleasantness of the speech is thence.

@3512. Desire and delectation from pleasantness thence. Signified.

@3577. Delights of good, and pleasantnesses of truth... @3589.

@5662[2]. Under <Peace>, see this reference. @HH 288. @289.

